  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Ether",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "One king succeeds another—Some of the kings are righteous; others are wicked—When righteousness prevails, the people are blessed and prospered by the Lord.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Shez, who was a descendant of Heth—for Heth had perished by the famine, and all his household save it were Shez—wherefore, Shez began to build up again a broken people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "Ether 9:26 (25–29)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 10:1",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Shez did remember the destruction of his fathers, and he did build up a righteous kingdom; for he remembered what the Lord had done in bringing Jared and his brother across the deep; and he did walk in the ways of the Lord; and he begat sons and daughters.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 191,
            "end": 197,
            "text": "Ether 6:12 (1–12)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 10:2",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And his eldest son, whose name was Shez, did rebel against him; nevertheless, Shez was smitten by the hand of a robber, because of his exceeding riches, which brought peace again unto his father.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "Mosiah 10:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Mosiah 10:6.",
            "prettyString": "Mosiah 10:6",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mosiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 10,
                    "end": 10,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 6,
                        "end": 6
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 10:3",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that his father did build up many cities upon the face of the land, and the people began again to spread over all the face of the land. And Shez did live to an exceedingly old age; and he begat Riplakish. And he died, and Riplakish reigned in his stead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 10:4",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Riplakish did not do that which was right in the sight of the Lord, for he did have many wives and concubines, and did lay that upon men’s shoulders which was grievous to be borne; yea, he did tax them with heavy taxes; and with the taxes he did build many spacious buildings.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 134,
            "text": "Esth. 2:14; Jacob 3:5; Mosiah 11:2 (2–14)."
          },
          {
            "start": 218,
            "end": 221,
            "text": "Gen. 47:24."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Gen. 47:24.",
            "prettyString": "Genesis 47:24",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "genesis",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 47,
                    "end": 47,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 24,
                        "end": 24
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 10:5",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And he did erect him an exceedingly beautiful throne; and he did build many prisons, and whoso would not be subject unto taxes he did cast into prison; and whoso was not able to pay taxes he did cast into prison; and he did cause that they should labor continually for their support; and whoso refused to labor he did cause to be put to death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 134,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "TG Oppression; Tyranny."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
